# oracle: w194gneb_norm — the w194gneb_chain_conv case with thermo_modify norm yes: the energies are divided by the atom count
# (Min::energy_force), so the energy test of the minimizer and the PE columns of the table use the normalized energies.
# Measured with native LAMMPS: the same stops as w194gneb_chain_conv (Step 54 and Step 64) and the table rows equal native's at the
# printed precision (8 significant digits), max relative error 0 after rounding; unrounded, the largest difference is 4.2e-8
# (GradVc), the printed digits themselves. Engine 1.2 s.
# native: b332f28 (the installed lmp, SPIN and REPLICA packages)
# oracle-partitions: 4
# oracle-inputs: w194gneb_chain.data w194gneb_chain.final
# oracle-compare: rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 printed=8 skip=GradV3dottan
units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style spin
atom_modify map array
read_data w194gneb_chain.data
mass 1 55.845
pair_style spin/exchange 3.0
pair_coeff * * exchange 3.0 0.02726 0.2171 1.841
neighbor 0.1 bin
neigh_modify every 10 check yes delay 20
fix 1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.1 0.0 0.0 1.0 anisotropy 0.0001 1.0 0.0 0.0
fix_modify 1 energy yes
fix 3 all neb/spin 1.0
timestep 0.0001
thermo 10
thermo_style custom step pe
thermo_modify format float %.15g norm yes
min_style spin
min_modify alpha_damp 1.0 discrete_factor 10.0
neb/spin 1.0e-7 1.0e-3 60 60 10 final w194gneb_chain.final verbose
